<mxCell id="175" value="FINDING B1 (Med). The Geh step sends a WhatsApp Flow with NO buttons/sections. The /chat simulator (addChips) renders only buttons+sections, never &#x27;flow&#x27;. A human testing via /chat sees the prompt with no selectable option and must know to TYPE &#x27;Havan&#x27;. README still claims /chat &#x27;drives the full booking flow&#x27;. Drift." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="470" width="320" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
